36. MANDATORY UNIVERSAL FIXES — LESSONS FROM THE WORKING STUDENT FOLLOW-UP REACT BUILD
PRIORITY: This section is a binding clarification of sections 4–8, 16–21, 29–35 for EVERY future Prudle React conversion. It is application-independent. Never copy the Student Follow-up UI, collections, filenames, or data logic into another app. The goal is to prevent a technically successful React build from failing to start after deployment.

36.1 ESTABLISH A WORKING BASELINE BEFORE REACT CONVERSION
- Inspect the complete supplied original application and the actual working deployment example, if provided.
- Distinguish the original HTML application, the compiled React build, the host page, and the deployed Worker. Do not assume that a problem in one is caused by another.
- Inventory exact runtime session keys, original login/logout behavior, Worker requests, UID mapping, timestamp formats, domain/origin assumptions, script order, and asset paths.
